 involving two gamorians  squaring off with vibro axes inside  something resembling a boxing ring  these pig-faced aliens made their star  wars debut in 1983's return of the jedi  posing as guards for the gangster jabba  the hutt  with the underworld kingpin long gone  from the time of the mandalorian  it appears his former palace rogues are  doing their best to make ends meet  along them were a handful of weak way  which just so happens to be the same  race as mopel goes rather than bartender  who just so happens to be played by w.l  brown who played the bartender dan  doherty  on hbo's deadwood opposite timothy  oliphant who happens to play marshall  kobanth in this  episode of the mandalorian but we're  getting ahead of ourselves  after concluding his lesson cordial  meeting with koresh mando and his  foundling make their way to tatooine to  look for the supposed mandalorian  wandering the planet's sandy dunes of  course they can't get a good look around  the planet from the razor crest  so they enlist the hangar of peli motto  who first appeared in the mandalorian's  inaugural season  alongside her crew of pitroids but  they're not the only droids running amok  as a familiar face pops up to help mando  navigate tatooine's perilous terrain  motto sought the map of tatooine inside  an r5 astromech unit  that fans of a new hope likely  recognized immediately in a new hope  luke skywalker goes after purchase from  the jawas a new droid for the family  moisture farm and the red and white r5d4  was his first choice  sadly the little guy didn't get to go  off and have galaxy-wide adventures with  the future jedi thanks to a bad  motivator  so that spark went to the fan favorite  r2d2 it's good to see that motto could  fix him up  even if he's a bit sluggish for her  liking now take your time  seriously you just can't get good help  anymore  the vast majority of season 2's first  episode takes place on tatooine which is  one of the most important locations in  the star 